Provided are 12 raw data files (_1 suffix) describing clinical trials, 5 of these datasets come from EudraCT (https://eudract.ema.europa.eu/) the European Union Drug Regulating Authorities Clinical Trials Database (which have either a EUCTR prefix, or no prefix in the case of the raw files) and 7 come from ClinicalTrials.gov (https://clinicaltrials.gov) a database created by the U.S. National Institutes of Health (all with an NCT prefix).
Evolvus curates these data for Oncogen, our database of genomic modifications in cancer, which is comprised of this clinical trial data, data from pubmed articles describing genetic and molecular modifications and data from drug labels on investigational and approved therapies. For this Evolvus manually annotates information describing the disease, drug, genes/genetic modifications, the patients enrolled in the trial and the trial conducted. These data are provided in a json format, all with the suffix _2.
These data can be further enriched by the addition of data from other sources, for example the drug labels (which describe drug modality and mechanism of action i.e. the target(s)) and mapped to ontologies. This should facilitate the matching of entities across trials for example, we could group trials by disease or phase, or drugs by modality or target. These data are also provided in json format, all with the suffix _3
